// Duck parade: Five giant rubber ducks (3.5 u) drift in a convoy along a network route from one
// end of the level to the other at 5 u/s (45 s max; over when the last duck reaches the end),
// ignore rock, absorb projectiles and push ships aside (no damage). Belt levels: the ring's
// centre line, retrograde. Positions are a function of the start tick, the route bytes and the
// level, so the client predictor knows them exactly.
// Behaviour: crates/ls-sim/src/events/duck_parade.rs (B3). Schema: `ls_sim::events::EventDef`.
EventDef(
    id: "duck_parade",
    name: "Duck parade",
    enabled: true,
    weight: 1.0,
    active_secs: 45.0,
    moods: [Giddy],
    params: {
        "ducks": 5.0,
        "duck_radius": 3.5,
        "speed": 5.0,
        // Distance between neighbouring ducks along the route (u).
        "spacing": 9.0,
    },
)
